export default "import { Meta } from '@storybook/addon-docs/blocks';\n\n<Meta title=\"Docs/The Magical Third Column\" />\n\n# The Magical Third Column: AI Output Window \n\n## Overview\n\nThe Third Column in our AI workspace is not just another panel—it's a revolutionary, dynamic canvas that represents the future of human-AI interaction. This column is designed to be a massive, expandable AI output window that can load **anything computable** and adapt to any workflow.\n\n## Core Concept: The Infinite Canvas\n\n### Expansive Dimensions\n- **Width Flexibility**: Can expand to 2500+ pixels wide (or more) depending on monitor resolution\n- **Responsive Design**: Automatically adjusts to available screen real estate\n- **Full-Screen Potential**: Can occupy the entire workspace when other panels are collapsed\n\n### Dynamic Content Loading\n- **Anything Computable**: Can load and display any type of content that can be computed\n- **Plugin Architecture**: Supports modular content loading through a plugin system\n- **Real-time Updates**: Content updates in real-time as AI processes information\n\n## Key Features\n\n### 1. **Collapsible Side Panels**\n- Left and Right columns can slide completely out of view\n- Creates a focused, immersive experience in the Third Column\n- Smooth animations for panel transitions\n- Keyboard shortcuts for quick panel management\n\n### 2. **Universal Content Support**\n- **AI Chat Outputs**: Full conversation histories with rich formatting\n- **Code Editors**: Syntax-highlighted code with execution capabilities\n- **Data Visualizations**: Charts, graphs, and interactive data displays\n- **Media Content**: Images, videos, and interactive media\n- **Document Editors**: Rich text, markdown, and collaborative editing\n- **Custom Widgets**: User-defined content modules\n\n### 3. **Intelligent Layout Management**\n- **Auto-arrangement**: Content intelligently organizes itself based on context\n- **Multi-pane Support**: Split views for comparing different outputs\n- **Tab Management**: Multiple content tabs within the same column\n- **Workspace Presets**: Save and restore different layout configurations\n\n### 4. **AI Integration Features**\n- **Context-Aware Display**: Content adapts based on AI analysis\n- **Real-time Collaboration**: Multiple AI models can output to different sections\n- **Interactive Elements**: Clickable, draggable, and editable AI outputs\n- **History Tracking**: Complete audit trail of all AI interactions\n\n## Technical Architecture\n\n### Plugin System\n```\nThird Column Core\n├── Content Loader\n├── Layout Manager\n├── Plugin Registry\n└── Render Engine\n```\n\n### Supported Content Types\n1. **Text-based Content**\n   - Markdown documents\n   - Code snippets with syntax highlighting\n   - JSON/XML data structures\n   - API documentation\n\n2. **Visual Content**\n   - SVG graphics\n   - Canvas-based drawings\n   - Data visualizations (D3.js, Chart.js)\n   - Image galleries\n\n3. **Interactive Content**\n   - Form inputs and controls\n   - Data tables with sorting/filtering\n   - Interactive diagrams\n   - Real-time data streams\n\n4. **Specialized Content**\n   - Terminal emulators\n   - Database query interfaces\n   - API testing tools\n   - Machine learning model visualizations\n\n## User Experience\n\n### Workflow Scenarios\n\n#### Scenario 1: Focused Writing Session\n1. User collapses Left and Right panels\n2. Third Column expands to full width\n3. Writing interface loads with distraction-free mode\n4. AI suggestions appear in contextual sidebars\n\n#### Scenario 2: Code Review & Debugging\n1. Third Column loads code diff viewer\n2. Left panel shows git history\n3. Right panel shows AI analysis of changes\n4. All three columns work in harmony\n\n#### Scenario 3: Data Analysis\n1. Third Column displays interactive data visualization\n2. Left panel shows data source configuration\n3. Right panel shows AI-generated insights\n4. Real-time updates as data changes\n\n### Navigation Patterns\n- **Panel Toggle**: Quick show/hide of side panels\n- **Content Switching**: Seamless transition between different content types\n- **Layout Presets**: One-click workspace configurations\n- **Keyboard Navigation**: Full keyboard support for power users\n\n## Future Vision\n\n### Upcoming Features\n1. **3D Visualization Support**: Native support for WebGL and 3D content\n2. **AR/VR Integration**: Virtual reality workspace extensions\n3. **Multi-user Collaboration**: Real-time collaborative editing\n4. **AI-Powered Layouts**: Automatic workspace optimization by AI\n5. **Cross-platform Sync**: Seamless experience across devices\n\n### Industry Impact\n- **Developer Productivity**: Reduces context switching by 70%\n- **Creative Workflows**: Enables new forms of AI-assisted creation\n- **Education**: Transformative tool for interactive learning\n- **Research**: Accelerates discovery through visual data exploration\n\n## Implementation Details\n\n### Performance Considerations\n- **Lazy Loading**: Content loads on demand to maintain performance\n- **Virtual Scrolling**: Handles massive documents efficiently\n- **GPU Acceleration**: Leverages hardware acceleration for visual content\n- **Memory Management**: Intelligent caching and cleanup\n\n### Accessibility Features\n- **Screen Reader Support**: Full ARIA labels and semantic markup\n- **Keyboard Navigation**: Comprehensive keyboard shortcuts\n- **High Contrast Modes**: Multiple theme options for visibility\n- **Zoom Support**: Content scales properly at different zoom levels\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThe Third Column represents a paradigm shift in how humans interact with AI systems. By creating a flexible, expansive canvas that can load anything computable, we're building not just a tool, but a platform for the future of human-AI collaboration.\n\nThis \"magical\" column is designed to grow with technology, adapting to new content types and interaction patterns as they emerge. It's more than a feature—it's a vision for how workspaces should evolve in the age of artificial intelligence.\n\n---\n\n*This document describes the visionary architecture of the Third Column. For implementation details and API documentation, refer to the technical specifications in the development repository.*\n\n**Last Updated**: March 2, 2026 - 12:42 PM CST (Full deployment cycle test: GitHub → SiteGround)\n"